  "arborg.B.agenda.0.text": "Lower property taxes for households and reduce the burden on residents — advocate reductions during the electoral term.",
  "arborg.B.agenda.0.title": "Property taxes",
  "arborg.B.agenda.1.text": "Present a comprehensive long-term plan that ensures the steady development of Árborg in consultation with residents.",
  "arborg.B.agenda.1.title": "Long-term plan",
  "arborg.B.agenda.2.text": "Maintain and improve quality services in schools, preschools and welfare services — the foundations of a strong municipality.",
  "arborg.B.agenda.2.title": "Quality services",
  "arborg.B.agenda.3.text": "Support a diverse economy in the Selfoss area, strengthening agriculture, tourism and innovation.",
  "arborg.B.agenda.3.title": "Economic development",
  "arborg.B.agenda.4.text": "Responsible and professional financial management that creates room for development without increasing debt excessively.",
  "arborg.B.agenda.4.title": "Responsible finances",
  "arborg.B.list.1.bio": "Matthías Bjarnason is a technician living in the Selfoss area and has served as a deputy municipal councillor for Framsókn in Árborg. He has written about property tax issues and family welfare and leads Framsóknarflokkurinn's B-list in Árborg in the 2026 municipal elections.",
  "arborg.B.list.1.interests.0": "Lower property taxes",
  "arborg.B.list.1.interests.1": "Preschools and home payments",
  "arborg.B.list.1.interests.2": "Infrastructure development",
  "arborg.B.list.1.interests.3": "Services for residents",
  "arborg.B.list.1.interests.4": "Employment issues",
