  "mulathing.M.agenda.0.text": "Progress on Fjarðarheiðargöng and the development of Axarvegur are top priorities for safety and settlement.",
  "mulathing.M.agenda.0.title": "Transport matters",
  "mulathing.M.agenda.1.text": "Strengthen business and ensure sound planning matters across all districts of Múlaþing.",
  "mulathing.M.agenda.1.title": "Business and planning",
  "mulathing.M.agenda.2.text": "A strong education system with early support and a genuine focus on children is fundamental.",
  "mulathing.M.agenda.2.title": "A strong education system",
  "mulathing.M.agenda.3.text": "The living conditions of senior citizens must be secure and dignified throughout the municipality.",
  "mulathing.M.agenda.3.title": "Living conditions for senior citizens",
  "mulathing.M.agenda.4.text": "Primary healthcare and general health services must be accessible to all residents.",
  "mulathing.M.agenda.4.title": "Accessible primary healthcare",
  "mulathing.M.agenda.5.text": "Responsible financial management and sensible use of shared public funds should characterize the next term.",
  "mulathing.M.agenda.5.title": "Responsible financial management",
  "mulathing.M.list.1.bio": "Lárus Bjarnason is a lawyer and served as district commissioner in Austurland for more than thirty years — first in Norður-Múlasýsla from 1989, then as district commissioner in Austurland from 2015 until he left office in autumn 2024 upon reaching the age limit. He is a person with extensive knowledge of law and administration in Austurland. Lárus leads the Centre Party's candidate list in Múlaþing in the 2026 elections.",
  "mulathing.M.list.1.interests.0": "The rule of law and policing",
