  "mulathing.M.list.5.occupation": "Preschool principal",
  "mulathing.M.list.6.bio": "Viðar Gunnlaugur Hauksson is a managing director and is in 6th place on the Centre Party's list in Múlaþing for the municipal elections in May 2026.",
  "mulathing.M.list.6.occupation": "Prog, ",
  "mulathing.M.list.7.occupation": "Teacher",
  "mulathing.M.list.8.bio": "Gestur Bergmann Gestsson is a farmer and is in 8th place on the Centre Party's candidate list in Múlaþing for the municipal elections in May 2026.",
  "mulathing.M.list.8.occupation": "Farmer",
  "mulathing.M.list.9.occupation": "Shift supervisor",
  "mulathing.M.tagline": "Múlaþing for the future — a community for all generations",
  "mulathing.V.agenda.0.text": "Protect the nature of Austurland and establish clear rules for environmentally sustainable development.",
  "mulathing.V.agenda.0.title": "Nature conservation",
  "mulathing.V.agenda.1.text": "Support a diverse economy — not only heavy industry but also knowledge-based industries, tourism and the creative sectors.",
  "mulathing.V.agenda.1.title": "Diversity in the economy",
  "mulathing.V.agenda.2.text": "Strengthen work in health, education and social affairs as the foundation of a strong community in Austurland.",
  "mulathing.V.agenda.2.title": "Jobs in social sectors",
  "mulathing.V.agenda.3.text": "Aim for carbon neutrality in the municipality’s operations and promote quality of life for future generations.",
  "mulathing.V.agenda.3.title": "Sustainable development",
  "mulathing.V.agenda.4.text": "Strong health and welfare services with an emphasis on equal opportunities for all residents, regardless of where they live.",
  "mulathing.V.agenda.4.title": "Health and quality of life",
  "mulathing.V.list.1.bio": "Ásrún Mjöll Stefánsdóttir is a carpenter from Seyðisfjörður and has served on the Múlaþing municipal council for VG. She has campaigned for environmental issues in Austurland; among other things, she proposed installing monitoring equipment to measure air pollution in Múlaþing’s harbours caused by cruise ships in Seyðisfjörður. She leads the joint list of VG and independents in Múlaþing in the 2026 elections.",
