  "nordurping.B.agenda.0.text": "Framsókn wants to offer free 36-hour preschool attendance to support families facing economic pressure.",
  "nordurping.B.agenda.0.title": "Free 36-hour preschool",
  "nordurping.B.agenda.1.text": "Ensure equal access to preschool without financial barriers — both a matter of justice and an investment.",
  "nordurping.B.agenda.1.title": "Equal access to preschool",
  "nordurping.B.agenda.2.text": "Increase flexibility in home-care payments to parents of children up to 18 months of age.",
  "nordurping.B.agenda.2.title": "Flexible home-care payments",
  "nordurping.B.agenda.3.text": "Solutions should support not only families but also preschool staff themselves.",
  "nordurping.B.agenda.3.title": "Support for staff",
  "nordurping.B.agenda.4.text": "Strong communities are built on strong families — a cornerstone of Framsókn’s priorities in Norðurþing.",
  "nordurping.B.agenda.4.title": "Strong communities, strong families",
  "nordurping.B.list.1.bio": "Eysteinn Heiðar Kristjánsson is project manager for ambulance services at the North Iceland Health Institution (HSN) in Húsavík. He leads Framsókn’s B-list in Norðurþing in the 2026 municipal elections and is chairman of the Framsókn association of Þingeyingar.",
