  "rangarthingeystra.D.list.9.occupation": "Football Coach and Grounds Manager",
  "rangarthingeystra.D.tagline": "Independence Party in Rangárþing eystra — development and stability",
  "rangarthingeystra.NRE.agenda.0.text": "Ensure the availability of plots for diverse business activities and attract more public-sector jobs and institutions. Create a workplace cluster in cooperation with companies, and market Rangárþing eystra as an attractive location for remote work.",
  "rangarthingeystra.NRE.agenda.0.title": "Employment",
  "rangarthingeystra.NRE.agenda.1.text": "Improve accessibility on walking paths and to shops (including Krónan’s smart store), strengthen home care services, and fight for an HSU home hospital in Rangárþing. Expand driving services by car at Kirkjuhvoll/VISS and create real opportunities for disabled people to participate in sports and leisure activities.",
  "rangarthingeystra.NRE.agenda.1.title": "Issues concerning disabled people, people with disabilities, and senior citizens",
  "rangarthingeystra.NRE.agenda.2.text": "Forward-looking planning, increased maintenance of rural roads, and completion of the town centre on Hvolsvöllur and Austurvegur. Include the Ring Road as a 2+1 road in the municipal plan, improve phone and internet connections, and develop walking, cycling, and riding paths on Hvolsvöllur, in Skógar, and in rural areas. A leisure bus between Hvolsvöllur and Hella, and bus fares between Hella and Hvolsvöllur reduced to ISK 690 (equivalent to fares in the Capital Region).",
  "rangarthingeystra.NRE.agenda.2.title": "Planning, transport, and infrastructure",
  "rangarthingeystra.NRE.list.1.bio": "Tómas Birgir Magnússon leads the NRE list in Rangárþing eystra in the 2026 municipal elections.",
  "rangarthingeystra.NRE.list.1.occupation": "Tourism operator and sports teacher",
  "rangarthingeystra.NRE.list.10.bio": "Guðbjörg Konráðsdóttir is a business graduate, residing at Hlíð in Rangárþing eystra. She is in 10th place on the N-list, the New Independent List, in Rangárþing eystra for the municipal elections on 16 May 2026. The list is a new independent candidacy led by Tómas Birgir Magnússon.",
  "rangarthingeystra.NRE.list.10.occupation": "Business economist",
  "rangarthingeystra.NRE.list.11.occupation": "Tour guide",
  "rangarthingeystra.NRE.list.12.occupation": "Shoemaker",
  "rangarthingeystra.NRE.list.13.occupation": "Construction technologist",
  "rangarthingeystra.NRE.list.14.occupation": "Candidate",
  "rangarthingeystra.NRE.list.2.bio": "Inger Erla Thomsen is a specialist at UNICEF Iceland and is in 2nd place on the N-list of the New Independent List in Rangárþing eystra for the municipal elections on 16 May 2026.",
  "rangarthingeystra.NRE.list.2.occupation": "Specialist at UNICEF",
