  "rangarthingytra.D.list.9.occupation": "Project manager",
  "rangarthingytra.D.tagline": "The Independence Party in Rangárþing ytra — stability and progress",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.agenda.0.text": "The aim is for Rangárþing ytra to become the country’s first carbon-neutral municipality.",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.agenda.0.title": "Carbon-neutral municipality",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.agenda.1.text": "Neighbourhood councils will be established to ensure residents have the greatest possible influence, and municipal council meetings will be broadcast live.",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.agenda.1.title": "Resident democracy",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.agenda.2.text": "Issues concerning children and young people will be prioritised in the allocation of funds, while safeguarding strong and outstanding school operations.",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.agenda.2.title": "Education and children first",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.agenda.3.text": "The goal is to install a pedestrian bridge at the old bridge site and improve transport infrastructure in the area.",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.agenda.3.title": "Infrastructure development",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.agenda.4.text": "Pressure will be applied to ensure that Landsvirkjun establishes permanent operations in the municipality alongside the Hvammsvirkjun development.",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.agenda.4.title": "Employment and Landsvirkjun",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.1.bio": "Eggert Valur Guðmundsson is self-employed and leads the A-list in Rangárþing ytra in the 2026 municipal elections; he has served on the municipal council for five terms since 1998.",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.1.occupation": "Self-employed",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.10.occupation": "Shop owner",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.11.bio": "Daníel Freyr Steinarsson is a contractor and firefighter and is in 11th place on the Á-list, an independent municipal candidacy founded in 2010, in Rangárþing ytra for the municipal elections on 16 May 2026.",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.11.occupation": "Contractor and firefighter",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.12.bio": "Auður Erla Logadóttir is a teacher and football coach in Rangárþing ytra. She works as head coach of youth divisions at Knattspyrnufélag Rangæinga (KFR) and has coached the club's boys' under-13 team. Auður Erla is in 12th place on the Á-list, an independent municipal candidacy in Rangárþing ytra, for the municipal elections on 16 May 2026.",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.12.occupation": "Teacher and football coach",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.13.bio": "Gabríel Snær Ólafsson is a plumbing apprentice. He is in 13th place on the Á-list in Rangárþing ytra for the municipal elections on 16 May 2026.",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.13.occupation": "Plumbing apprentice",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.14.occupation": "Candidate",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.2.bio": "Margrét Harpa Guðsteinsdóttir is a farmer at Lambhagi on Rangárvellir, where she lives with her husband and four children and where they farm. She has served on the municipal council of Rangárþing ytra for the Á-list and is in 2nd place on the Á-list in Rangárþing ytra for the municipal elections on 16 May 2026.",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.2.occupation": "Farmer and municipal councillor",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.3.bio": "Erla Sigríður Sigurðardóttir is an ambulance worker and has worked for the South Iceland Healthcare Institution since 2016. She grew up in Mosfellsbær but moved to Hella in 2014 and lives there in Heiðvangur with her two daughters. Erla has been studying leadership at the University of Akureyri in recent years and is active in rescue and civil protection work: a member of the Hella Air Rescue Team, on the regional board of rescue teams in Rangárvalla- and Vestur-Skaftafellssýsla, and on the South Iceland Civil Protection operations management team. Her priority issues are a family-friendly community, sports and prevention work, and traffic and safety matters. Erla is in 3rd place on the Á-list in Rangárþing ytra for the 2026 municipal elections.",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.3.occupation": "Paramedic",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.4.bio": "Viðar Már Þorsteinsson, often called Viddi, was born and raised in Hella and has worked as a technical representative for 26 years at Míla (formerly Síminn). He moved back to Hella in 2014 and works remotely from there. Viðar is an Á-list municipal council member in Rangárþing ytra during the current term and has long held positions of trust for his trade union. He emphasizes resident democracy and the development of youth sports. Viðar is in 4th place on the Á-list (RYA) for the municipal elections on 16 May 2026.",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.4.occupation": "Technical officer and municipal councillor",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.5.bio": "Eiríkur Vilhelm Sigurðarson is the factory manager of Samverk in Hella, a tourism studies graduate with a master's degree in project management. He worked as Rangárþing ytra's marketing and promotions officer in 2015 and has since been involved in a wide range of projects in the municipality. Eiríkur is chairman of the Geysir Equestrian Association and served on the executive committee of the National Horse Show at Rangárbakkar in 2022. He was executive director of the Njáluvaka cultural festival in Hella and Hvolsvöllur, which was attended by close to ten thousand people. Eiríkur is in 5th place on the Á-list in Rangárþing ytra and is the list's candidate for municipal manager in the 2026 municipal elections.",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.5.occupation": "Factory manager",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.6.bio": "Guðbjörg Snorradóttir is a certified bookkeeper and developmental therapist. She is in 6th place on the Á-list, an independent municipal candidacy founded in 2010 that currently holds the majority on the municipal council of Rangárþing ytra, for the 2026 municipal elections. The list's candidate for municipal manager is Eiríkur Vilhelm Sigurðarson, who is in 5th place.",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.6.occupation": "Bookkeeper and development assistant",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.7.bio": "Þórunn Dís Þórunnardóttir is an incubation manager and serves on the municipal council of Rangárþing ytra for the Á-list. She is in 7th place on the Á-list in Rangárþing ytra for the 2026 municipal elections. The Á-list was founded in 2010, is independent of national political parties, and currently holds the majority on the municipal council.",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.7.occupation": "Hatchery manager and municipal councillor",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.8.bio": "Gunnar Aron Ólason is an information officer and is in 8th place on the Á-list, an independent municipal candidacy founded in 2010, in Rangárþing ytra for the 2026 municipal elections.",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.8.occupation": "Information officer",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.list.9.occupation": "On parental leave",
  "rangarthingytra.RYA.tagline": "Á-listinn — an objective, independent movement-based policy for a sustainable and democratic Rangárþing ytra",
