  "reykjavik.M.list.4.bio": "Hlédís Maren Guðmundsdóttir is a sociologist, born in 1992 or 1993. She served on the board of Ung vinstri-græn from 2013 to 2015 and completed a BS degree in sociology from Háskóli Íslands. She worked as a journalist and wrote articles for Heimildin in 2020–2021, and later at Útlendingastofnun. In recent years, she has written critical opinion pieces and shifted to the right in her political views.",
  "reykjavik.M.list.4.interests.0": "Abolish the city's human rights office",
  "reykjavik.M.list.4.interests.1": "Opposition to gender impact assessments of city services",
  "reykjavik.M.list.4.interests.2": "Housing issues and the rental market",
  "reykjavik.M.list.4.interests.3": "Prioritising core services over ideological projects",
  "reykjavik.M.list.4.interests.4": "Education policy and individual quality assessment",
  "reykjavik.M.list.4.occupation": "Sociologist",
  "reykjavik.M.list.40.occupation": "Housewife",
