  "seltjarnarnes.D.agenda.3.text": "Develop Eiðistorg as a vibrant hub for services and community gatherings in the town.",
  "seltjarnarnes.D.agenda.3.title": "Eiðistorg",
  "seltjarnarnes.D.list.1.bio": "Þór Sigurgeirsson is the Mayor of Seltjarnarnes and leads the D-list in the 2026 municipal elections; he is educated in sales and marketing and has served as Mayor since 2022.",
  "seltjarnarnes.D.list.1.occupation": "Mayor",
  "seltjarnarnes.D.list.10.occupation": "Business graduate",
  "seltjarnarnes.D.list.11.occupation": "Chief Financial Officer",
  "seltjarnarnes.D.list.12.occupation": "Librarian",
  "seltjarnarnes.D.list.13.occupation": "Former MP",
  "seltjarnarnes.D.list.14.bio": "Petrea Ingibjörg Jónsdóttir, commonly known as Peta, is the former office manager of the Independence Party. She began working at the party office in the summer of 1982, first as a temporary telephone operator, and worked there continuously for about 37 years, until the end of 2019. As office manager, she was responsible, among other things, for the party's membership register and the administration of meetings and events. Petrea served on the Seltjarnarnes town council for the Independence Party from 1990 to 1998 and had previously been an alternate council member from 1986. She has been active in party work for more than 65 years, ever since she helped distribute the party newspaper Framtak in Akranes during the 1959 elections. Her father, Jón Árnason, was a town councillor in Akranes and a member of parliament for Vesturland from 1959 to 1977. Petrea is in 14th place on the Independence Party's list in Seltjarnarnes for the 2026 municipal elections.",
  "seltjarnarnes.D.list.14.occupation": "Candidate",
  "seltjarnarnes.D.list.2.occupation": "Managing Director",
  "seltjarnarnes.D.list.3.bio": "Magnús Benediktsson is an economist and works as a specialist in the audit division at PwC. He holds a BSc degree in economics and a master’s degree in auditing and accounting. Magnús is 25 years old and lives on Kirkjubraut in Seltjarnarnes with his partner, Hildur Sif Hilmarsdóttir, and they are expecting their first child in May. He has been active in the Independence Party since the age of seventeen, is chair of Baldur, the association of young Independence Party members in Seltjarnarnes, and serves on the parish committee of Seltjarnarneskirkja. Magnús ran for 3rd place in the Independence Party primary in Seltjarnarnes in February 2026 and now holds 3rd place on the D-list in the 2026 municipal elections.",
  "seltjarnarnes.D.list.3.occupation": "Economist",
  "seltjarnarnes.D.list.4.occupation": "Economist",
  "seltjarnarnes.D.list.5.occupation": "Director",
  "seltjarnarnes.D.list.6.bio": "Dagbjört Snjólaug Oddsdóttir is a district court attorney and one of the owners of the law firm Könnun Legal ehf., where she works as general counsel. She completed a master’s degree in law at the University of Iceland in 2010 and obtained litigation rights in 2012. Her areas of expertise are maritime and transport law, insurance law, and corporate and commercial law. Dagbjört has lived in Seltjarnarnes for many years and has taken an active part in the Independence Party there, including as a board member of Sjálfstæðisfélag Seltirninga and a representative on the sports and leisure committee. She previously sought a leading place on the party’s list for the 2022 elections and is now in 6th place on the Independence Party’s list in Seltjarnarnes for the municipal elections on 16 May 2026.",
  "seltjarnarnes.D.list.6.occupation": "Lawyer",
  "seltjarnarnes.D.list.7.bio": "Agnes Sólbjört Helgadóttir is a law student and is in 7th place on the Independence Party's list in Seltjarnarnes for the municipal elections on 16 May 2026. The list was unanimously approved by the representative council of the Independence associations in Seltjarnarnes at the end of February 2026.",
  "seltjarnarnes.D.list.7.occupation": "Law student",
  "seltjarnarnes.D.list.8.occupation": "Business economist",
  "seltjarnarnes.D.list.9.occupation": "PE teacher",
