  "skaftarhreppur.SKO.list.1.bio": "Jóhannes Gissurarson is a farmer at Herjólfsstaðir in Álftaver and the leader of the municipal council in Skaftárhreppur. He has been prominent in discussions on civil protection, evacuation plans, and communication between municipalities and state institutions, including in the aftermath of the glacial flood in Skálm in the summer of 2024, when he criticized the authorities’ response and called for improved telecommunications in the area. He leads the Þróttur list in the 2026 municipal elections.",
